cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use causekit in research, please cite the software and the exact version used."
type: software
title: "CauseKit: Identification-aware causal inference and instrumental variables for Python"
abstract: >-
  An identification-aware Python toolkit for causal inference. Version 0.7.0a3
  provides IV, randomized effects, cross-fitted nuisance orchestration,
  IPW/AIPW ATE, ATT, and ATC, auditable nearest-neighbor matching with fixed- or
  supported estimated-score inference, conventional staggered difference-in-differences, and cross-fitted
  covariate-adjusted efficient PT-All event-study estimation, and native partially linear
  double machine learning and separately contracted honest R-/DR-learning.
authors:
  - family-names: Akanbi
    given-names: "Oluwajuwon Mayomi"
version: 0.7.0a3
repository-code: "https://github.com/Akanom/causekit"
url: "https://github.com/Akanom/causekit"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - causal inference
  - econometrics
  - instrumental variables
  - two-stage least squares
  - 2SLS
  - randomized experiments
  - inverse probability weighting
  - difference-in-differences
  - event studies
  - causal machine learning
  - double machine learning
  - identification
